Subject: ECON/NANO/PHIL Defending Post-Scarcity

Some things that will remain scarce, unless the very laws
of physics are overturned, or humans are turned into
self-genociding zombies with no ambitions to expand their
range of capability:

* Matter (protons, neutrons, electrons, etc.)
* Real estate (surface area, cubic, etc.)
* Time (speed of light limit) -- transportation, communication,
	computation
* Energy & thermodynamic disequilibrium ("extropy")

None of these things can be copied like software.

