   the lifestyles of kalihari bushmen optimal, we would wonder why it
   was that we would be encroaching on the bushmen and not vice versa.

Agricultural cultures can maintain a population density 10 times or
higher that of foraging cultures.  Thus agricultural cultures can
exterminate foraging cultures fairly effectively via war or other
forms of encroachment.  (The success of the hard-work agricultural
meme-o-type depends on its contribution to collective aggression as
well as individual efficiency.)

For example, in North America, the Europeans displaced the natives
fairly effectively, but in Latin America, the Europeans conquered the
natives, but did not really eliminate them genetically or culturally.
The difference is that the Latin American natives had better-developed
agriculture and had high enough population densities to be difficult
to completely kill or displace.

